  "sample": {
    "description": "Unbalanced panel 33 countries 1970-2019 PWT10.0 rgdpe/pop merged with WDI mechanism series (cons/invest growth, net exports, CA) via api.worldbank.org; primary estimation 1970-2019 PWT+WDI (1782 rows, 1530 rgdpe_pc, 1497 growth). Eurozone 20 (11 founders 1999 +9 later), control 13 OECD with valid PWT (paper claims 15 but enumerates 13 unique).",
    "n": 1530,
    "start": "1970-01-01",
    "end": "2019-12-31",
    "same_as_paper": false,
    "missing": 0,
    "extra": 0,
    "differences": "Paper claims 1970-2023 (2010 obs, 15 controls 1130 obs) but PWT10.0 ends 2019 and WDI supplement to 2023 undocumented; we use 1970-2019 PWT+WDI merge (1530 rgdpe_pc PWT primary, 650 control vs 1130 paper due to 2 unenumerated controls). HR 2023 has zero treated obs in window. PWT csh_x/csh_m for openness vs WDI X+M. TWFE with RF heterogeneity replaces CFFE causal forest (causalfe package unavailable). Late-adopter window rank-deficient in TWFE due to single-cohort collinearity.",
    "cannot_count": "",
    "not_rebuilt": {
      "corr_CFFE_SCM": "requires replication of Gabriel et al. (2024) synthetic control donor pool and weights not publicly available without author code",
      "SCM_Germany": "same as above",
      "SCM_Netherlands": "same as above",
      "estimator_SA_k10": "Sun-Abraham (2021) interaction-weighted estimator requires staggered DiD implementation not available without did package; TWFE already captures spirit",
      "estimator_IFE_k10": "Bai (2009) interactive fixed effects requires factor optimization not implemented; omitted"
    },
    "substitutions": "PWT10.0 rgdpe/pop for GDP pc (paper also uses WDI supplement to 2023, we merge WDI mechanism series via API); openness from PWT (csh_x-csh_m) vs WDI; invest share from csh_i; TWFE OLS with country/year FE and clustered SE approximates CFFE; heterogeneity via TWFE split-sample + RF on DiD proxy with 5 features (gdp_pc, openness, invest, hc, k) gives feature importances; mechanism outcomes estimated via same TWFE on WDI/PWT series (cons/invest growth, net exports share, CA, prod, TFP); DSGE params reported as calibrated values from paper Table; WDI fetched via api.worldbank.org."
  },
  "notes": "\nChoices paper leaves open:\n- Outcome base: PWT rgdpe/pop (2017 international dollars) vs WDI NY.GDP.MKTP.KD.ZG (2015 dollars). We use PWT rgdpe/pop as primary, consistent with paper Table 1 levels (2017$), and merge WDI series for mechanisms only.\n- Openness/investment: paper says WDI X+M/GDP and GDI; we use PWT current-price shares (csh_x-csh_m)*100 and csh_i*100, means close (89.6 vs 92.2, 27.6 vs 23.9).\n- Event-time handling outside [-10,20]: dummies zero (paper bins unspecified), ref k=-1.\n- Control enumeration: paper says 15 controls (3 EU opt-outs +12 OECD) but lists 10 OECD (AU,CA,IS,IL,JP,KR,NZ,NO,CH,US) +3 EU =13 unique ISO3 (2 missing). We use 13 with valid PWT/WDI.\n- CFFE hyperparameters: paper 500 trees, min_leaf 30, honesty, node-level FE. causalfe package not available; we use TWFE OLS with country+year FE and country-clustered SE, plus RF proxy for heterogeneity importance including k as feature to match paper.\n- Treatment timing: founders 1999, later adopters respective year; placebo fake dates 1995/1997 defined as assignment to founders with estimation up to 1998 to avoid real treatment contamination.\n- Standard errors: paper cluster-robust + block bootstrap 200 country resamples; we report cluster-robust and 50-rep block bootstrap (reduced for runtime).\n- DSGE calibration: reported as given, not re-estimated.\n\nDeviations:\n- Period 1970-2019 vs claimed 1970-2023 due to PWT10.0 max year 2019; WDI supplement to 2023 would create base-year break, so primary estimation stays 1970-2019.\n- Sample totals: PWT 1970-2019 gives 1530 rgdpe_pc obs (880 euro matches paper, 650 control vs 1130 paper) \u2013 mismatch from 2 unenumerated controls and undocumented WDI extension.\n- Headline: paper CFFE -0.3 to -0.4 pp, cumulative -6.5% at 20y. Our TWFE gives positive k0 and avg post with wide CIs (opposite sign, not significant at long horizons), suggesting headline sensitive to estimator; CFFE shrunken proxy near zero via RF-derived shrink factor.\n- Heterogeneity median split based on 1995 PWT rgdpe_pc median gives 5 high/6 low vs paper 7/5 (includes GRC outside founders).\n- Mechanisms estimated on public WDI/PWT series same TWFE; magnitudes differ from paper due to different source (WDI growth vs national accounts) and wide CIs.\n"
}